{"gold":[{"independent_answer":"160","question_sha256":"da974d9282e2d4d7a54f3ba490e84582c87e50e3ebeecac536aee5a6651208aa","reason":"The subsidized employee costs 22 - 6 = 16 dollars per hour, which is 4 dollars per hour cheaper than 20 dollars per hour. Over 40 hours, the savings are 4 × 40 = 160 dollars.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-6397"},{"independent_answer":"underdetermined","question_sha256":"5b8a1e1b353b90511059a81d0247a5c54e0d6e70425e3598a3167fdc9ce7b1d0","reason":"Housesitting earns 15 × 10 = 150 dollars. Dog walking is paid at 22 dollars per hour, but the question gives three dogs rather than the number of dog-walking hours. The gold 216 assumes one hour per dog, which is not stated.","status":"AMBIGUOUS","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1977"},{"independent_answer":"567","question_sha256":"bb949d2f6df0004a8ad590d83f58fe0f64416860c0ffb7c2c4616fce6206df2b","reason":"Mowing earns 6 × 63 = 378 dollars, weed pulling earns 11 × 9 = 99 dollars, and mulching earns 9 × 10 = 90 dollars. Their sum is 378 + 99 + 90 = 567.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-990"},{"independent_answer":"700","question_sha256":"d5bdc882e9b37aa267eb6d311e3902edac5fff2f26239e83d4193bbce2beb149","reason":"The father's hole is 4 × 400 = 1600 feet deep. Michael's target depth is 2 × 1600 - 400 = 2800 feet, requiring 2800 ÷ 4 = 700 hours at the same rate.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1885"},{"independent_answer":"350","question_sha256":"481a11f8f17baa3d974d840ba4d9a7251b040ee2461d11081bf7602bc407606a","reason":"John descends 10 × 5 = 50 feet, so his new elevation is 400 - 50 = 350 feet.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-3716"},{"independent_answer":"2","question_sha256":"f6ac7af8444f6c6d2f694351d277e017f95d9c7f41ec5bc165cd6be1f258bde7","reason":"The files total 80 + 90 + 70 = 240 megabits. At 2 megabits per minute they take 240 ÷ 2 = 120 minutes, and 120 ÷ 60 = 2 hours.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5981"},{"independent_answer":"5","question_sha256":"bfd8